# @boundary rejects invalid left-hand side to assignment
# @boundary-pending BUG-320  compound index assignment still emits the read form as an LHS
#
# The COMPOUND half of BUG-320, still broken after the plain-assignment fix and pinned so it
# cannot be forgotten. Every compound branch in genAssign emits `genExpr(a.target)` on the
# left, which for an index target is `_zbr_at(recv, i)` -- a function call.
#
# Deliberately NOT fixed in the same pass: four of the twelve compound operators (`//=`,
# `**=`, `<<=`, `>>=`) carry their own lowerings a few lines further down genAssign, so
# routing indexes through them means either duplicating those lowerings -- which is the
# copy-the-decision shape that CAUSED BUG-320 -- or restructuring genAssign, which deserves
# to be its own change rather than being smuggled into a regression fix.
#
# This passes today by requiring the refusal, and FAILS when compound assignment is fixed --
# the signal to rewrite it as a positive test, not to re-baseline.

def main()
    var xs: List(int) = List(int)()
    xs.add(5)
    xs[0] += 3
    print(xs[0])
